/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119776","id":4543202579,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDsvFEw","user":{"login":"bd65-crt","id":271831608,"node_id":"U_kgDOEDPSOA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/271831608?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt","html_url":"https://github.com/bd65-crt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-26T10:07:59Z","updated_at":"2026-05-26T10:07:59Z","body":"This is the simplest version I can think of. The problem seems straightforward.\n\n[mrp2.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/28259319/mrp2.zip)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4543202579/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4543927496","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119776#issuecomment-4543927496","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119776","id":4543927496,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDtbUyA","user":{"login":"markdibarry","id":21325943,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzI1OTQz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21325943?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/markdibarry","html_url":"https://github.com/markdibarry","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markdibarry/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markdibarry/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markdibarry/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markdibarry/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markdibarry/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markdibarry/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markdibarry/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markdibarry/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markdibarry/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-26T11:58:32Z","updated_at":"2026-05-26T12:07:04Z","body":"Maybe I don't understand the issue? From your MRP, the repeatable area is not set up correctly when at zoom x1, x2, or x3, so I would expect this to be the behavior. Your screen size is 1920x1080, but your repeat is 256x256\n\n<img width=\"1403\" height=\"771\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b3e5625b-8107-4b9d-908c-e2844eb1c15b\" />\n\nIf you set it up correctly, you get this:\n\n<img width=\"1011\" height=\"597\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2f47b41e-ee07-4e2d-82d2-e73df062b69a\" />\n\nZoom 1x:\n<img width=\"1093\" height=\"736\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2d4b0cd2-34bd-4589-a54b-38782bd36504\" />\n\nZoom 2x:\n<img width=\"1087\" height=\"741\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c4738419-37a4-43f4-b388-dbf0efb7fb2e\" />\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4543927496/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4544043378","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119776#issuecomment-4544043378","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119776","id":4544043378,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDtiZcg","user":{"login":"bd65-crt","id":271831608,"node_id":"U_kgDOEDPSOA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/271831608?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt","html_url":"https://github.com/bd65-crt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-26T12:28:38Z","updated_at":"2026-05-26T12:28:38Z","body":"Actually, I think the inconsistency between the editor page and the actual running page is the problem: there is a serious offset, which can obviously be solved by expanding the scope and repeating, but it will undoubtedly cause trouble and waste resources. This is the problem I encountered during the game development process, and then I traced it to the source code. In fact, there is an error in the unit of mathematical operation here.\nI think the repeat area may explain why the symptom becomes more visible, but after tracing the source code, I don't think it is the root cause.\nThe underlying issue appears to be a coordinate-space mismatch:\n**`camera_screen_center` is world-space** (camera_2d.cpp:58):\n```cpp\ncamera_screen_center = xform.affine_inverse().xform(0.5 * screen_size);\n```\n`affine_inverse()` of the camera transform maps screen pixels → world coordinates. So the result is world-space.\n\n**`screen_size * 0.5` is screen pixels** — confirmed by how `get_camera_transform()` converts it to world-space at line 165:\n```cpp\nPoint2 screen_offset = (screen_size * 0.5 * zoom_scale); // zoom_scale = 1/zoom\n```\nWhen the engine needs `screen_size * 0.5` in world-space, it **always** multiplies by `zoom_scale`. The original code at line 66 (before my fix) was the **only place** that didn't.\n\n**The bug (line 66, before fix):**\n```cpp\nPoint2 adj_screen_pos = camera_screen_center - (screen_size * 0.5);\n// world coordinate         −  screen pixels          ← dimension mismatch\n```\n\nThis is not about repeat area setup. It's a straightforward unit mismatch between world and screen coordinates.\nIf repeat area were the root cause, changing repeat size should change correctness.\nBut here, the computation itself changes with zoom, even before repeat wrapping happens, which suggests the problem occurs earlier in the pipeline.\ndo you think im right?\nAnd some images when zoom = 0.5.\n\nCould you please reconsider whether this is a coordinate-space bug rather than a repeat-area configuration issue?\n\n<img width=\"2022\" height=\"1460\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c445bfb4-d878-4f89-9412-81e58cef990d\" />\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4544043378/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4544072169","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119776#issuecomment-4544072169","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119776","id":4544072169,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDtkJ6Q","user":{"login":"bd65-crt","id":271831608,"node_id":"U_kgDOEDPSOA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/271831608?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt","html_url":"https://github.com/bd65-crt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-26T12:35:18Z","updated_at":"2026-05-26T12:35:18Z","body":"In my first version of the MRP using C#, I used some methods to debug and print out the relevant coordinates, and tried to fix the issue at the script level according to my ideas. I believe it met the expectations.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4544072169/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4544095264","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119776#issuecomment-4544095264","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119776","id":4544095264,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDtlkIA","user":{"login":"markdibarry","id":21325943,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzI1OTQz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21325943?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/markdibarry","html_url":"https://github.com/markdibarry","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markdibarry/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markdibarry/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markdibarry/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markdibarry/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markdibarry/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markdibarry/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markdibarry/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markdibarry/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markdibarry/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-26T12:40:15Z","updated_at":"2026-05-26T12:40:15Z","body":"This still sounds like expected behavior. If you read over the [parallax 2d tutorial](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/2d/2d_parallax.html) you can understand where you made some mistakes. Again, your repeats are set up incorrectly even with your changes. Your changes would also not be a fix, but just a change to the workflow, which is a breaking change. If you're having issues with previewing in the editor, there is the plugin linked at the bottom of the tutorial or [this PR to add it built in](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111832).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4544095264/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4544408772","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119776#issuecomment-4544408772","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119776","id":4544408772,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDt4sxA","user":{"login":"bd65-crt","id":271831608,"node_id":"U_kgDOEDPSOA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/271831608?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt","html_url":"https://github.com/bd65-crt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-26T13:22:16Z","updated_at":"2026-05-26T13:22:16Z","body":"I may not have explained my concern clearly.\n\nI understand that increasing repetition (`repeat_times`) can work around the visible issue, and I have read the documentation on that.\n\nMy point is different: `camera_screen_center` is in **world space**, while `screen_size * 0.5` is in **screen space**. You can compare this with line 165 in the same file, where `screen_size * 0.5` is explicitly converted using `zoom_scale` before being used in world-space calculations.\n\nSo from my reading, the only difference here is that this line lacks the `zoom_scale` conversion.\n\nMy concern is that although repetition can hide the visible offset, it does so by requiring additional repeated rendering. For some projects with stricter performance or memory constraints, that extra rendering is exactly what I was trying to avoid by investigating this.\n\nYou mentioned that my proposed change would be breaking. From my perspective, it seems more like an internal consistency fix: it doesn't change the public API or intended feature set, only makes the coordinate calculation consistent.\n\nWould you mind explaining where you see the breaking behavior? It is possible we are misunderstanding each other, and I’d like to understand your concern better.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4544408772/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4544467093","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119776#issuecomment-4544467093","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119776","id":4544467093,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDt8QlQ","user":{"login":"bd65-crt","id":271831608,"node_id":"U_kgDOEDPSOA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/271831608?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt","html_url":"https://github.com/bd65-crt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bd65-crt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"crea